# Typecheck the whole project. Deliberately NOT a per-edit agent hook: it costs
# ~40s here, which would stall the agent loop on every Write/Edit. Per-edit
# formatting and scoped tests live in .claude/settings.json instead.
#
# `astro check`, not `tsc --noEmit`. This hook shipped with tsc and a note saying
# "promote astro check if a template type error ever slips through" — one did:
# src/pages/pets/index.astro indexed an enum-keyed Record with a `string`, which
# `astro build` does not check and `tsc --noEmit` does not see inside a .astro
# template. astro check covers BOTH the templates and the .ts files, so it
# replaces tsc here rather than being added alongside it.
#
# It was also worth nothing until 2026-09-07: husky was a devDependency with a
# hook file but no `prepare` script, so core.hooksPath was never set and this
# hook had never run. Three type errors reached main that way. If it stops
# firing again, check `git config core.hooksPath` first — an unset value means
# `npm install` (or `npx husky`) has not wired it in this clone.
npx astro check
